@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Confirm navigation away from unsaved input
actor "Account holder" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "Domain form" as form
  participant "Routed page or form dialog\n(FormDraft)" as page
  participant "UnsavedChangesGuard" as guard
  participant "UnsavedChangesDialog" as dialog
  participant "ApplicationShell /\nRouter / focus" as router
  participant "ISessionService /\nSessionService" as session
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "Protected API" as api
end box

== Draft state (L2-031.4) ==
form -> page : draftChange(DraftState { dirty, pending, unconfirmed, summary }) on every change
page -> page : A form dialog or routed form page keeps the latest DraftState as draft(); a routed page hosting form dialogs delegates draft() to its open dialog, clean when none is open; a routed form page that also hosts form dialogs (the sprint plan) combines its own draft with its open dialog's: dirty, pending or unconfirmed when either is, with a summary naming both; a ProjectLayoutPage child page falls back to the layout's open dialog

== Route change with a draft: another destination, a router link inside a dialog, browser Back, or Sign out (L2-031.4) ==
actor -> router : Choose another destination, a router link inside an open dialog (such as View existing lead), Back, or Sign out
router -> guard : canDeactivate(page), registered on every route whose page is a form or hosts form dialogs
guard -> page : Read draft(): pending, unconfirmed and dirty
guard -> guard : reason = SignOut when the destination is /login (Sign out navigates with replaceUrl and state { signOut: true }, which the /login guard lets through while the session is still held), otherwise Navigate
alt Clean draft
  guard -> router : Proceed: open the destination or sign out
  router --> actor : Focus destination heading (L2-033.4)
else Save pending
  note right of page
    Save shows progress and ignores repeat clicks;
    Cancel and Close are disabled while it is pending (L2-031.2).
  end note
  guard -> guard : Hold the route change until the save resolves
  alt Save succeeds
    page --> guard : Baseline updated; draft clean
    guard -> router : Proceed to the destination
    router --> actor : Saved result announced; focus destination heading
  else Save rejected or fails
    page --> guard : Draft kept with field errors (one error focuses its field, several the error summary) or the save error; still dirty
    guard -> dialog : Continue as for a dirty draft
  end
else Dirty draft, not pending
  guard -> dialog : confirm(reason, draft().summary)
  dialog -> router : Trap focus; start on the safe choice (L2-033.2)
  router --> actor : Title and choices follow the reason; the dialog names what would be lost when the form supplies a summary, otherwise generic copy
  alt Stay or Escape
    actor -> dialog : Stay on this page / Stay signed in, or Escape
    dialog --> guard : close(Stay), or close() with no result, which counts as Stay
    guard --> router : Cancel the route change
    router --> actor : Restore focus to the trigger; draft intact, session kept
  else Discard
    actor -> dialog : Leave without saving / Sign out without saving
    dialog --> guard : close(Discard)
    guard -> router : Allow; the draft is dropped with its page and no save request is sent
    opt reason SignOut
      router -> session : ApplicationShell calls end(SignedOut); loginNotice = signed-out
    end
    router --> actor : Focus destination heading; sign-out opens sign-in with "You've signed out"
  end
end
note right of router
  Once a navigation completes that deactivates the page
  hosting an open application dialog, the dialog closes
  with no result (dismissed), so its opener changes
  nothing; a cancelled navigation leaves it open with
  its draft. A query-only Back or Forward that reuses
  the hosting page runs no canDeactivate and leaves the
  dialog open with its draft. ProjectLayoutPage defers
  its own re-navigation until its dialog closes.
end note

== Cancel, Close, or Escape in a form dialog (L2-031.4) ==
actor -> page : Cancel, Close, or Escape (disabled while a save is pending)
page -> page : Read its own draft(); the guard is not involved
alt Clean draft
  page -> router : Close the dialog
  router --> actor : Focus returns to the dialog's trigger (L2-033.2)
else Dirty draft
  page -> dialog : confirm(CancelForm, draft().summary)
  dialog -> router : Trap focus; start on Keep editing
  router --> actor : "Discard your changes?"; names what would be lost when the form supplies a summary, otherwise generic copy
  alt Keep editing or Escape
    dialog --> page : close(Stay), or no result (Escape): Stay
    page --> actor : Focus back in the form; every value intact
  else Discard changes
    dialog --> page : close(Discard)
    page -> page : Close without a save request: no result (dismissed), or Outdated when the form had reported its page out of date; the discard changes no saved record
    page -> router : Focus the trigger or a surviving contextual control
  end
end

== Session ends while a draft is dirty or a save is pending or unconfirmed (L2-003.4) ==
alt Proactive expiry at the token's exp
  session -> session : end(Expired)
else Any protected request answered 401 at the current generation N
  api --> session : 401 through sessionInterceptor
  session -> session : end(Unauthorized), once for generation N
  session --> page : A save answered 401 rejects with it: not saved, pending false; a dirty draft stays dirty, and a form with no input (status change, confirmation) is never dirty
end
session -> session : Generation N+1; token and capability summary cleared; in-flight requests aborted; ToastService clears its toasts
note right of session
  An aborted save may still have committed;
  cancellation never implies that it did not.
end note
session --> router : endReason changed; ApplicationShell stores requestedPath, sets loginNotice session-ended, navigates to /login with replaceUrl
router -> guard : canDeactivate(page)
guard -> page : Read draft(): pending, unconfirmed and dirty (a hosting page reads its open dialog's draft)
guard -> guard : endReason set: no unsaved-changes dialog (nothing can be saved without a session)
alt A save was aborted: its promise rejects with SessionEndedError, so pending stays true, or the last save got no response and is still unconfirmed
  guard -> router : loginNotice = session-save-unknown; leave
  router --> actor : Sign-in shows "Your session ended while a save was in progress"; check the record after signing in
else Dirty draft, never sent or answered 401 at generation N (not SessionEndedError)
  guard -> router : loginNotice = session-unsaved; leave
  router --> actor : Sign-in shows "Your session ended before your changes were saved"
else Clean draft: no FormDraft reports a pending or unconfirmed save (a board move, reorder, status control, or other mutation without a FormDraft may have been in flight)
  guard -> router : loginNotice stays session-ended; leave
  router --> actor : Sign-in shows "Your session ended"; after sign-in the restored view rereads, showing whether that mutation committed
end
router -> router : Leaving the shell destroys the form, its dialog and page, and route-scoped providers
note over router, api
Late responses of generation N are discarded: no state update and no second session end.
Neither notice reports a successful save.
end note

note over page, api
Cancellation and discarded input send no mutation request.
Reload or tab close uses the browser's own unload prompt instead of UnsavedChangesDialog.
end note
@enduml
